# =============================================================================
# WAL record framing — 17-byte record header + type-specific payload.
# Source of truth: src/persistent_artrie/core/wal/codec.rs
#   RECORD_HEADER_SIZE = 17 = CRC32(4) + Length(4) + LSN(8) + Type(1).
# The 15 WalRecordType discriminants are listed below; full semantics live in
# the accompanying wal-format.md table.
# =============================================================================

  WAL record  -  17-byte header + payload

  byte 0     4      8                 16 17
      +------+------+-----------------+--+================================+
      |crc32 |length|       lsn       |ty|   payload (length bytes,       |
      | u32  | u32  |       u64       |u8|   type-specific encoding)      |
      +------+------+-----------------+--+================================+
       :      :                        :
       :      :                        '- type: one of 15 WalRecordType tags
       :      '- length: payload byte count
       '- crc32: integrity over (length, lsn, type, payload)

  WalRecordType:
      1 Insert      4 BeginTx     7 Increment   10 BatchInsert    13 VersionDurable
      2 Remove      5 CommitTx    8 Upsert      11 BatchIncrement 14 VersionGc
      3 Checkpoint  6 AbortTx     9 CompareAndSwap 12 VersionUpdate 15 CommitRank
